<title>UK: Iceland plans share buyback at 105p/share.</title>
<headline>Iceland plans share buyback at 105p/share.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British frozen food chain Iceland Group Plc said on Wednesday it planned to cut its share capital by cancelling 35 percent of its ordinary shares at a price of 105p per share.</p>
<p>The company also said 37.5 percent of its convertible preference shares would be cancelled at a price of 96p per share.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
